3. FUNCTIONAL INTERPRETATION OF CORE INTERACTORS

MDM2 — E3 Ubiquitin-Protein Ligase
Acts as an important negative regulator of TP53 by promoting its ubiquitination and degradation under normal cellular conditions.

ATM — Ataxia-Telangiectasia Mutated Kinase
Participates in the cellular response to DNA damage and contributes to TP53 activation and stabilization.

CHEK2 — Checkpoint Kinase 2
Participates in DNA-damage signaling and contributes to TP53-mediated checkpoint responses.

BRCA1 — Breast Cancer Type 1 Susceptibility Protein
Participates in DNA repair and genome-maintenance pathways that functionally interact with TP53-mediated responses.

EP300 — E1A-Associated Protein p300
Functions as a transcriptional co-regulator and interacts with TP53 to influence gene expression.
