5. BIOLOGICAL SIGNIFICANCE

The interaction network highlights TP53 as a central regulatory component connecting DNA-damage signaling, cell-cycle control, transcription, and DNA repair.
For example:

ATM / CHEK2 → DNA-Damage Signaling → TP53 Activation
MDM2 → TP53 Regulation and Degradation
EP300 → Transcriptional Regulation
BRCA1 → DNA Repair and Genome Maintenance

Together, these interactions demonstrate how multiple proteins cooperate to regulate cellular responses to stress and DNA damage.
