6. KEY TAKEAWAY

TP53 functions as an important hub within a network of proteins involved in maintaining genomic stability and controlling cellular responses to DNA damage.
The STRING analysis helped me understand how protein-protein interaction networks can provide a broader biological context for individual genes or proteins.
Rather than studying TP53 as an isolated protein, the PPI network shows how its function is connected to multiple regulatory pathways and interacting proteins.
